---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, REPO_URL } from "../config";
---

<Legal
  title="Support"
  description="How to get help with Barklog, and how to delete your account or get a copy of your data."
  updated="5 September 2026"
>
  <p>
    Barklog is made and run by one person, so support is me reading my email. Below is what I
    get asked most, and how to reach me when it isn't there.
  </p>

  <h2>Getting in touch</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. I'm one person, so give me a
    couple of days.
  </p>
  <p>If something is broken, the report I can act on tells me:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>which iPhone, and which version of iOS</li>
    <li>the Barklog version, from the App Store listing's version history</li>
    <li>what you did, what you expected, and what happened instead</li>
  </ul>
  <p>A screenshot is usually worth all three.</p>

  <h2>Reporting a bug</h2>
  <p>
    Barklog is open source. Bugs and feature requests can go straight to
    <a href={`${REPO_URL}/issues`} rel="noreferrer">the issue tracker</a>, which is where I
    work from and where you can see whether something is already known.
  </p>
  <p>
    That tracker is public and anyone can read it. If your problem involves your email address,
    your account, or anything else you'd rather not publish, email me instead.
  </p>

  <h2>Deleting your account</h2>
  <p>
    Tap your avatar in the toolbar — it's there on every tab — and choose to delete your
    account. That removes your account, your backlog, and your subscription record. It happens
    immediately and it can't be undone.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Deleting your account does not cancel an App Store subscription.</strong>
    Cancel that in your Apple subscription settings, or you'll keep being billed for an account
    that no longer exists.
  </p>

  <h2>Getting a copy of your data</h2>
  <p>
    There's no export button yet. Email me and I'll put together everything stored about you
    and send it over within 30 days. The <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> lists what that
    covers.
  </p>

  <h2>A game is missing, or its details are wrong</h2>
  <p>
    Every cover, release date, platform and summary in Barklog comes from
    <a href="https://www.igdb.com" rel="noreferrer">IGDB</a>, a games database maintained by its
    community, and Barklog passes it along as it is. So a game Barklog can't find is usually a
    game IGDB doesn't have yet, and a wrong release date is wrong upstream too.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can add or correct an entry on IGDB directly, and it'll reach Barklog within a day or
    so. If something shouldn't be in Barklog at all, email me — I'll take it out and report it
    upstream.
  </p>

  <h2>A shared video matched the wrong game</h2>
  <p>
    Share a YouTube or TikTok video to Barklog and it works out which game the video is about
    from the title and the channel name alone. It's a guess, and it goes wrong most often
    within a series, where the titles barely differ. Check what came back before you add it.
    Nothing is saved to your backlog until you do.
  </p>

  <h2>You can't sign in</h2>
  <p>
    Sign-in runs through Clerk. If it stalls or bounces you back, close Barklog and open it
    again — that clears a sign-in that got stuck halfway through. If you're still locked out,
    email me with the address you signed up with and I'll look at the account from my side.
  </p>
</Legal>
